MATCH qftx-positive-real-linear-monad-normal-forms [{"id":"qftx-positive-real-linear-monad-normal-forms","title":"Positive real linear monad normal forms","kind":"A","category":"quantum-field-theory-mathematics","library":"mathematics","order":967.26,"companion":"qftx-positive-real-linear-monad-normal-forms-examples","requires":["relations-functions-and-quotients","compact-laplace-type-operators-and-hodge-representatives","grothendieck-spectral-sequences-and-computations","cohomology-of-quasi-coherent-sheaves-on-affine-and-projective-schemes","qftx-adhm-linear-data-and-framed-monads"],"items":[{"id":"thm-qftx-positive-real-adhm-monad-normal-form","kind":"theorem","domain":"mathematics","library":"mathematics","title":"Positive real linear monad normal forms","reference":"items/thm-qftx-positive-real-adhm-monad-normal-form.md#Statement","deps":["def-axiom-of-choice","def-complex-manifolds-and-holomorphic-vector-bundles","thm-first-hypercohomology-spectral-sequence","thm-cohomology-projective-space-twisting-sheaves","def-qftx-adhm-linear-data-stability-and-regularity","thm-qftx-adhm-real-complex-quotient-correspondence"],"dependency_roles":{"def-axiom-of-choice":"mathematical-premise","def-complex-manifolds-and-holomorphic-vector-bundles":"mathematical-premise","thm-first-hypercohomology-spectral-sequence":"mathematical-premise","thm-cohomology-projective-space-twisting-sheaves":"mathematical-premise","def-qftx-adhm-linear-data-stability-and-regularity":"mathematical-premise","thm-qftx-adhm-real-complex-quotient-correspondence":"mathematical-premise"},"statement":"Assume AC. On CP3 with coordinates (λ1,λ2,μ1,μ2) and σ=(-barλ2,barλ1,-barμ2,barμ1), let O(-1)⊗U→O⊗K→O(1)⊗U′ be a linear bundle monad with dimensions k,2k+N,k, N≥2, locally free middle cohomology F, trivial on every real line μ1=z1λ1−barz2λ2,μ2=z2λ1+barz1λ2, and unitary framing on λ=0. Give F a nondegenerate holomorphic σ-Hermitian pairing whose induced forms on real-line sections are positive. Then there are normalized internal Hermitian spaces and chain identifications giving α=(A,C,Jλ1+I†λ2)T, β=(-C,A,Iλ1−J†λ2), A=B1λ1−B2†λ2−μ1, C=B2λ1+B1†λ2−μ2, with raw zero moments and stable-and-costable regularity. Normalized framed real monad isomorphisms correspond exactly to simultaneous U(k) action and inverse extraction recovers that orbit. For compact rotations (λ1,t1t2λ2,t1μ1,t2μ2), the chain factors are (t1t2)^-1,diag(t2^-1,t1^-1,h),1, matching raw framing weights e_a^-1. The construction is natural for framed first-order families in the exact locally-free/base-change range; it includes k=0 and reducible/flat summands. This is an intrinsic normal form, not an equivalence with an incorrectly dimensioned historical displayed block.","strategy":"Complete the explicit obligations in dependency order; no source invocation or conditional declaration is a proof.","proof_strategy":"direct","axiom_base":"ZF + full AC inherited through named sheaf/cohomology and matrix suppliers; exact uses must be recorded.","provenance":{"statement":"literature-derived","proof":"not-supplied"},"sources":{"references":[{"title":"Simon K. Donaldson, The ADHM construction of Yang–Mills instantons","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2205.08639","locator":"Sections3–6, printedpp4–11, actually read; roadmap invokes Penrose and real normal forms and is not a complete proof of these proposed suppliers."}]},"proof_contract_plan":{"state":"Unproved local established-theory authoring obligation","obligations":["Lift the positive holomorphic σ-reality isomorphism and its involutive identities to the monad, proving existence/uniqueness up to the precise chain homotopies.","Show positivity of the induced internal normalizations from real-line positivity, without simply assuming the middle Hermitian form positive.","Normalize the leading μ matrices and real structure by explicit linear/unitary transformations; prove all required transversality and constant-rank statements.","Extract exact raw moment coefficients, prove regularity and the equivalence of full-rank and stable/costable conditions in these conventions.","Prove residual changes are exactly U(k), inverse extraction uniqueness, framing, compact rotations and first-order-family compatibility.","Keep global charge normalization explicit: finite O(m) resolution and line-class comparison identify algebraic and topological Chern characters; the positive incidence point/fiber Thom calculation gives π*u=H²."],"full_statement_not_narrowable_to_evade_obligations":true,"native_authoring_and_review_required":true},"page":"qftx-positive-real-linear-monad-normal-forms","category":"quantum-field-theory-mathematics","status":"draft","origin":"pipeline","inventory_expansion_required":true,"design_state":"Owner-approved unproved mathematical prerequisite proposal; fresh native supplemental drift and full authoring required.","proof_obligation":"Complete the explicit obligations in dependency order; no source invocation or conditional declaration is a proof.","dependency_level":1}],"status":"draft","scaffold":true
