research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/canonical-followup-before/items__def-qftx-instanton-equivariant-partition-series.md:47:Fix integers $N\geq2$ and $k\geq0$ and a real stability parameter $\zeta>0$. Let $V=\mathbb C^k$ and $W=\mathbb C^N$ with Hermitian structures. The positive-FI stable complex ADHM quotient $X_{k,N}^\zeta$ is the geometric quotient by $GL(V)$ of quadruples $(B_1,B_2,I,J)$ with $B_i\in\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb C}(V)$, $I:W\to V$, and $J:V\to W$, satisfying $[B_1,B_2]+IJ=0$ and the condition that the vectors $B_{i_1}\cdots B_{i_m}I(w)$ span $V$ for all words of length $m\geq0$ and $w\in W$. This is the positive stability chamber; it is not, by definition, the zero-FI regular quotient or the moduli space of anti-self-dual connections.
