research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/canonical-followup-before/items__pthm-qftx-omega-background-fixed-point-expansion.md:49:Fix $N\geq2$, $k\geq0$, and $\zeta>0$. Let $X_{k,N}^\zeta$ be the positive-FI stable complex ADHM quotient with rotation and dual-framing torus $T=(S^1)^2\times(S^1)^N$ acting by $(t_1,t_2,h)\cdot(B_1,B_2,I,J)=(t_1B_1,t_2B_2,Ih^{-1},t_1t_2hJ)$, where $\mathbf W=\sum_{\alpha=1}^N e_\alpha^{-1}$. Write $\epsilon_i=c_1^T(t_i)$ and $a_\alpha=c_1^T(e_\alpha)$, and assume these weights are algebraically independent. Let $q$ be dimensionless and formal. For an $N$-tuple of partitions $\vec Y=(Y_1,\ldots,Y_N)$, each $Y_\alpha$ a finite downward-closed subset of $\mathbb Z_{\geq0}^2$, put $|\vec Y|=\sum_\alpha|Y_\alpha|$, $\mathbf V_{\vec Y}=\sum_{\alpha=1}^N e_\alpha\sum_{(i,j)\in Y_\alpha}t_1^it_2^j$, and $\mathbf W^\vee=\sum_\alpha e_\alpha$. Assume the complexified torus acts algebraically on a smooth separated finite-type variety of complex dimension $2kN$, with a finite invariant affine atlas and finite proper fixed locus. Assume the fixed points and tangent characters are exactly those of the positive-FI ADHM theorem. Extend $T$ by a flavor circle acting trivially on the quotient, with additive character $\widetilde m$, and let $\mathcal E_{\widetilde m}=c_{2kN}^{T_m}(TX_{k,N}^\zeta\otimes L_{-1})$ be the top Chern insertion for the inverse flavor line. Assume its localized Borel–Moore pushforward is defined by the proper-fixed-locus construction and satisfies the noncompact localization formula. For the source-reported N=2* convention, set $m=i m_E$ for real Euclidean mass $m_E$ and $\widetilde m=m+(\epsilon_1+\epsilon_2)/2$.
