research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/canonical-followup-before/research__advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-51.notes.md:14:A domain mismatch in upstream inputs was handled locally. `def-framed-u-n-instanton-moduli-and-adhm-data` restricts to `N≥2` (Statement line 35), while `thm-adhm-fixed-point-instanton-count` starts with `N≥1` (Statement line 48). The main series definition and physics theorem therefore use `N≥2`; the existing U(1) example is supported by the new self-contained `lem-qftx-u1-one-instanton-adhm-space`, which proves only the explicit `k=N=1` scalar quotient. I did not edit either upstream item. The owner should align the upstream theorem range with its ADHM definition or supply a general rank-one interface if the broader theorem range is intended.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/canonical-followup-before/research__advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-51.notes.md:20:| `def-qftx-instanton-equivariant-partition-series` | For positive-FI framed ADHM data with `N≥2`, define the coefficientwise formal N=2* series by the localized Borel–Moore pushforward of the inverse-flavor-line top Chern insertion. A tangent weight `w` contributes `w−m̃`; the complex orientation gives degree `4kN`, matching the normalized fundamental-class degree. Use `m=i m_E`, `m̃=m+(ε1+ε2)/2`; at S4, `m̃=i m_E+r⁻¹`. | `def-framed-u-n-instanton-moduli-and-adhm-data`; `def-qftx-localized-equivariant-borel-moore-data`; `def-qftx-proper-fixed-locus-localized-pushforward`; `post-qftx-s4-n2-localization-model` | 5 / `escalated` |
