research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/adhm-prerequisite-scaffold.md:13:Fix integers $N\ge1$ and $k\ge0$ and standard Hermitian spaces $V=\mathbb C^k$, $W=\mathbb C^N$. A framed ADHM linear datum is $x=(B_1,B_2,I,J)$ with $B_i\in\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb C}(V)$, $I:W\to V$ and $J:V\to W$. Define the complex and real polynomial expressions
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/adhm-prerequisite-scaffold.md:31:Assume AC. Fix $N\ge1$, $k\ge0$, $V=\mathbb C^k$ and $W=\mathbb C^N$ with their standard bases. Let $X$ be the stable locus in the complex ADHM equation $[B_1,B_2]+IJ=0$, where $B_i\in\operatorname{End}(V)$, $I:W\to V$, $J:V\to W$, and stability means that the vectors $B_{i_1}\cdots B_{i_m}I(w)$ span $V$. The action $g\cdot(B_1,B_2,I,J)=(gB_1g^{-1},gB_2g^{-1},gI,Jg^{-1})$ of $GL(V)$ on $X$ is free and proper. Its orbit quotient with quotient topology is a Hausdorff second-countable complex manifold of complex dimension $2kN$, with tangent space $\ker d_1/\operatorname{im}d_0$ for the infinitesimal ADHM deformation maps.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/adhm-prerequisite-scaffold.md:47:Assume AC. Fix $N\ge1$, $k\ge0$, standard Hermitian $V=\mathbb C^k$, $W=\mathbb C^N$ and ADHM data $x=(B_1,B_2,I,J)$ with the complex equation $[B_1,B_2]+IJ=0$. Stability means that the $B_1,B_2$ words applied to $I(W)$ span $V$; costability means no nonzero common invariant subspace of $V$ lies in $\ker J$; regular means both. Set
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/adhm-prerequisite-scaffold.md:75:Build the P2 diagonal Koszul resolution and the corresponding finite hypercohomology reconstruction. For a rankN torsion-free sheaf framed trivially on l∞ with Hilbert polynomial N binom(m+2,2)−k, prove the exact H0/H2 vanishing and H1 dimensions needed for the normalized three-term ADHM monad. Use coherent Ext-duality for torsion-free sheaves, not a locally-free-only Serre theorem. Prove the family/base-change form actually needed.
