research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/adhm-prerequisite-scaffold.md:219:For a smooth finite-atlas X with proper fixed locus F, define the localized BM pushforward p_*loc=pF*∘(i_*loc)−1, using the proved concentration isomorphism and genuine proper trace pF. State the domain/degree, coefficient field, fundamental-class versus unit convention and permitted insertions. This is a construction on actual BM classes, not a definition of the desired ADHM coefficient or an ordinary nonproper pushforward.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/adhm-prerequisite-scaffold.md:227:Prove the construction independent of the affine cover and compatible with proper equivariant maps with proper fixed loci; when p itself is proper it agrees with genuine proper pushforward. Use actual self-intersection and Thom purity to compute p_*loc(α cap[X])=sumF pF*((i*α/eTνF) cap[F]). For finite F this is the finite reciprocal Euler sum, with degree shifts and empty fixed set correct. The result applies to the separately proved smooth separated stable ADHM quotient and its finite invariant word-slice atlas/partition fixed locus, but those ADHM-specific facts are consumed later in old12 to avoid a page cycle.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/adhm-prerequisite-scaffold.md:269:The noncompact pair works with actual BM classes and proper fixed-locus trace. Eigenfunctions on finite invariant affine charts kill character actions; finite MV/excision proves concentration, and self-intersection derives the Euler denominator. No desired ADHM coefficient is used as a definition of its own integral. The original approved correspondence/pushforward obligations remain real until these new native proofs complete.
