research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/adhm-full-theorem-before-core.md:58:Assume full AC as inherited from the supplied instanton-charge convention. If a $T$-equivariant isomorphism from the positive-FI quotient to the moduli of framed rank-$N$ torsion-free coherent sheaves on $\mathbb{CP}^2$ with Hilbert polynomial $N\binom{m+2}{2}-k$ is supplied, it transfers the fixed-point classification and tangent characters to that Gieseker space. The ordinary framed anti-self-dual moduli space is a separate zero-FI regular locus: identifying that locus with the regular ADHM quotient is another unresolved conditional input, and no fixed-point count or equality of series is asserted for it. If a separately proved noncompact equivariant pushforward for $\mathcal M^\zeta_{k,N}$ has a localization identity with these isolated fixed points and tangent Euler classes, then its value on the unit is the coefficient displayed above. The compact ABBV formula alone does not establish such an identity: $\mathcal M^\zeta_{k,N}$ is noncompact for $k>0$. This theorem makes no identification with an ordinary continuum gauge-theory path integral.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/adhm-full-theorem-before-core.md:66:[[def-framed-u-n-instanton-moduli-and-adhm-data|Framed ADHM data and the positive-FI stable quotient]]
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/adhm-full-theorem-before-core.md:73:**Given:** $N\geq1$, $k\geq0$, $\zeta>0$, the Hermitian spaces $V,W$, the complex ADHM equation, the stability condition, and the $T$-action stated above. Assume full AC as in the Statement: the published algebraic quotient and fixed-scheme suppliers use AC, and the conditional Chern-class/Gieseker clause inherits AC. The finite word, matrix and character calculations themselves use only finite selections. All characters are treated as algebraically independent formal variables.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/adhm-full-theorem-before-core.md:75:[F1] [[def-framed-u-n-instanton-moduli-and-adhm-data]]: the ADHM equation is $[B_1,B_2]+IJ=0$, stability means the $B_1,B_2$-words applied to $I(W)$ span $V$, the quotient is by $GL(V)$, and $T$ acts by the displayed rotation and dual-framing convention.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/adhm-full-theorem-before-core.md:79:[F3] The stable complex ADHM equation locus has a free proper gauge action and a Hausdorff second-countable complex quotient of dimension $2kN$, with tangent $\ker d_1/\operatorname{im}d_0$. Word-frame slices give holomorphic quotient charts and explicit character gauge lifts at fixed points. [[lem-adhm-stable-quotient-and-torus-lift]]
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/adhm-full-theorem-before-core.md:83:[L1] [[thm-atiyah-bott-berline-vergne-integration-formula]] gives the real Borel fixed-component formula only for compact oriented smooth $T$-manifolds without boundary, including empty-locus vanishing in every dimension. This compact theorem supplies no noncompact pushforward for the ADHM quotient.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/adhm-full-theorem-before-core.md:85:[L2] [[def-framed-u-n-instanton-moduli-and-adhm-data]] defines the quotient presentations and the framed connection and sheaf spaces, but contains no ADHM/monad isomorphism between them. For the zero-FI clause, regular means stable and costable: no nonzero common $B_i$-invariant subspace lies in $\ker J$. This is the exact raw-data convention in [[def-qftx-adhm-linear-data-stability-and-regularity]]. The sheaf/ASD correspondences remain separate proof obligations; no such supplier is inferred from either definition.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/adhm-full-theorem-before-core.md:91:[A2] For the ordinary instanton dictionary in the Statement, assume a $T$-equivariant ADHM correspondence identifies the zero-FI regular quotient with the framed finite-action anti-self-dual moduli space, preserving the trace charge and framing. No fixed-point transfer from the positive-FI resolution to that open regular locus is assumed.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/adhm-full-theorem-before-core.md:97:1.1 The infinitesimal $GL(V)$ action and the derivative of the complex ADHM equation form the complex $$C^0=\operatorname{End}(V)\xrightarrow{d_0}C^1=\operatorname{End}(V)t_1\oplus\operatorname{End}(V)t_2\oplus\operatorname{Hom}(W,V)\oplus\operatorname{Hom}(V,W)t_1t_2\xrightarrow{d_1}C^2=\operatorname{End}(V)t_1t_2,$$ where $d_0(\xi)=([\xi,B_1],[\xi,B_2],\xi I,-J\xi)$ and $d_1(\dot B_1,\dot B_2,\dot I,\dot J)=[\dot B_1,B_2]+[B_1,\dot B_2]+\dot I J+I\dot J$. Expanding gives $d_1d_0(\xi)=[\xi,[B_1,B_2]+IJ]=0$, so this is a complex. [given, F1, algebra]
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/adhm-full-theorem-before-core.md:113:7.2 If assumptions [A1] and [A4] are supplied, the equivariant isomorphism transfers the fixed-point bijection and tangent characters to the Gieseker space. The local definition supplies no ADHM/monad proof of this comparison, as recorded in [L2]. [given, A1, A4, L2, step 6.1, step 6.2, algebra]
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/adhm-full-theorem-before-core.md:121:9.1 For $k>0$, use the tuple $Y_1=\{(i,0):0\leq i<k\}$ and $Y_\alpha=\varnothing$ for $\alpha>1$; step 6.1 constructs a stable datum. Replacing $B_1$ by $B_1+c\,\mathrm{id}_V$ preserves the complex equation and stability while changing $\operatorname{tr}(B_1)$ by $kc$ for every $c\in\mathbb C$. Trace is invariant under conjugation, so the descended trace function on the geometric quotient has image $\mathbb C$, which is not compact. Thus the quotient is noncompact. The completed Borel carrier matches the compact real-Borel interface in [L1]. The ADHM/monad comparisons [L2] and a valid noncompact pushforward remain the separate conditional inputs stated above. [given, F1, L1, L2, step 6.1, algebra] ∎
