research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/gaga-repair-before/research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-59.notes.md:61:Native Step 1 records are present for all 8 assigned items, with the three `ready` records hash-current: the definition, stable-quotient lemma and real/complex quotient theorem are `ready`; the GAGA theorem, Beilinson/framed-vanishing lemma, monad/ADHM theorem and both examples are `escalated`. The GAGA proof remains conditional on [A1] projective analytic local-flatness, Cartan A–B and uniform generation, and [A2] relative direct-image comparison. No local carriers with complete proofs for those packages exist. Its consumers retain their completed conditional arguments and must remain escalated until the actual interfaces are supplied and checked. Draft status, pending precheck, and absent independent approval were not treated as prerequisite gaps.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/gaga-repair-before/items/lem-adhm-stable-quotient-and-torus-lift.md:4:title: "Stable ADHM quotient charts, properness and torus lifts"
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/gaga-repair-before/items/lem-adhm-stable-quotient-and-torus-lift.md:50:Assume AC. Fix $N\ge1$, $k\ge0$, $V=\mathbb C^k$ and $W=\mathbb C^N$ with their standard bases. Let $X$ be the stable locus in the complex ADHM equation $[B_1,B_2]+IJ=0$, where $B_i\in\operatorname{End}(V)$, $I:W\to V$, $J:V\to W$, and stability means that the vectors $B_{i_1}\cdots B_{i_m}I(w)$ span $V$. The action $g\cdot(B_1,B_2,I,J)=(gB_1g^{-1},gB_2g^{-1},gI,Jg^{-1})$ of $GL(V)$ on $X$ is free and proper. Its orbit quotient with quotient topology is a Hausdorff second-countable complex manifold of complex dimension $2kN$, with tangent space $\ker d_1/\operatorname{im}d_0$ for the infinitesimal ADHM deformation maps.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/gaga-repair-before/items/lem-adhm-stable-quotient-and-torus-lift.md:64:[Nakajima–Yoshioka, §3.1: framed ADHM setting and fixed-point character conventions](https://arxiv.org/pdf/math/0311058)
