## Statement

Assume full AC. Then the analytic sheaf cohomology of $\mathcal O(-1)$ vanishes in every degree on $\mathbb P^r(\mathbb C)$ for $1\le r\le3$. The analytic cohomology of $\mathcal O(-2)$ vanishes in every degree on $\mathbb P^r(\mathbb C)$ for $r=2,3$. In particular, $H^0(\mathbb P^1,\mathcal O(-1))=0$ and $H^q(\mathbb P^3,\mathcal O(-2))=0$ for $q=0,1,2$. This is an analytic deduction from the named scalar-cohomology supplier and does not identify algebraic and analytic cohomology by GAGA.

## Statement references

[[thm-qftx-gaga-analytic-projective-dolbeault-scalar-cohomology]]

[[lem-qftx-positive-real-monad-hyperplane-twist-sequences]]

## Facts & Assumptions

**Given:** Full AC and the standard holomorphic hyperplane inclusions $\mathbb P^{r-1}\hookrightarrow\mathbb P^r$ for $1\le r\le3$.

[A1] Under full AC, the current batch-67 scalar cohomology theorem proves that for every $0\le r\le3$, $H^0(\mathbb P^r,\mathcal O)=\mathbb C$ and $H^q(\mathbb P^r,\mathcal O)=0$ for $q>0$. Its current Step 1 record is ready and hash-current. [[thm-qftx-gaga-analytic-projective-dolbeault-scalar-cohomology]]

[F1] For a hyperplane inclusion $i:\mathbb P^{r-1}\hookrightarrow\mathbb P^r$, multiplication by its defining linear form gives the exact holomorphic sequences
$0\to\mathcal O(-1)\to\mathcal O\to i_*\mathcal O_{\mathbb P^{r-1}}\to0$ and
$0\to\mathcal O(-2)\to\mathcal O(-1)\to i_*\mathcal O_{\mathbb P^{r-1}}(-1)\to0$.
[[lem-qftx-positive-real-monad-hyperplane-twist-sequences]]

## Proof

**Given:** [A1] and [F1]. All cohomology in this proof is analytic sheaf cohomology.

1.1 Fix $r\in\{1,2,3\}$. In the first sequence of [F1], the map $H^0(\mathbb P^r,\mathcal O)\to H^0(\mathbb P^{r-1},\mathcal O)$ is restriction of constants and hence is the identity $\mathbb C\to\mathbb C$. Exactness therefore gives $H^0(\mathbb P^r,\mathcal O(-1))=0$. The adjacent higher groups of $\mathcal O$ and $\mathcal O_{\mathbb P^{r-1}}$ vanish by [A1]; the long exact sequence then gives $H^q(\mathbb P^r,\mathcal O(-1))=0$ for every $q>0$. [given, A1, F1, algebra]

2.1 Fix $r\in\{2,3\}$. In the second sequence of [F1], both $\mathcal O_{\mathbb P^r}(-1)$ and $\mathcal O_{\mathbb P^{r-1}}(-1)$ are acyclic by step 1.1, since $r-1\in\{1,2\}$. Its long exact cohomology sequence therefore gives $H^q(\mathbb P^r,\mathcal O(-2))=0$ for every $q\ge0$, including the stated $\mathbb P^3$ groups. [given, F1, step 1.1, algebra] ∎

## Proof references

[[thm-qftx-gaga-analytic-projective-dolbeault-scalar-cohomology]]

Assume full AC. Let $k\ge0$ and
$N\ge2$. On $\mathbb P^3(\mathbb C)$ with homogeneous coordinates
$(\lambda_1,\lambda_2,\mu_1,\mu_2)$, set
$$
j(\lambda_1,\lambda_2,\mu_1,\mu_2)
=(-\bar\lambda_2,\bar\lambda_1,-\bar\mu_2,\bar\mu_1),
\qquad \sigma([z])=[jz].
$$
For each $(z_1,z_2)\in\mathbb C^2$, let $\ell_z$ be the real twistor line
defined by
$$
\mu_1=z_1\lambda_1-\bar z_2\lambda_2,\qquad
\mu_2=z_2\lambda_1+\bar z_1\lambda_2,
$$
and let $\ell_\infty=\{\lambda_1=\lambda_2=0\}$. Suppose
$$
\mathcal O(-1)\otimes U\xrightarrow{\alpha}
\mathcal O\otimes S\xrightarrow{\beta}
\mathcal O(1)\otimes U'
$$
is a complex of holomorphic vector bundles with $\beta\alpha=0$, locally split
injective and surjective end maps, and locally free middle cohomology
$F=\ker\beta/\operatorname{im}\alpha$ of rank $N$, where
$\dim_\mathbb C U=\dim_\mathbb C U'=k$ and
$\dim_\mathbb C S=2k+N$. Suppose $F|_{\ell_z}$ is holomorphically trivial for
every $z$, and it has a nondegenerate holomorphic $\sigma$-Hermitian pairing
whose induced first-slot-linear Hermitian form on
$H^0(\ell_z,F|_{\ell_z})$ is positive definite for every $z$. Here the
pairing means an isomorphism $h:F\to D(F)$ fixed by $D$, where for a
homogeneous linear matrix $P$ one sets $P^\#(z)=P(jz)^\dagger$ and the signed
